                                                    "desc:8":  "§5§lDO THIS§r\nRight-click the controller with the §9Hologram Projector§r. The whole campus appears as a ghost, in this order:\n\n  platform -\u003e silo -\u003e spine duct -\u003e spiral chamber -\u003e rotor assembly -\u003e cooling tower, cooling tower -\u003e vent stack -\u003e switchyard -\u003e extraction derrick -\u003e enrichment annex\n\n§2What the projection draws is exactly what the structure check wants.§r There is no build-only leniency left anywhere and no second controller to place. In survival the projector pulls blocks straight out of your inventory.\n\n[img height=500]btsquests:textures/gui/plant-overview.png[/img]\n\n§cWHAT THE PROJECTOR WILL NOT PLACE FOR YOU§r\nIt raises walls. It does not fit machines. When it has finished you still have to place, by hand:\n  §912x Turbine Housing§r - 4 in the spine bore, 8 on the gallery centreline. Those cells are left as §cAIR§r,\n     §8and they keep showing as ghosts for ever. That is the projector marking the spot, not a job it will finish.§r\n  §9every hatch, injector, sensor and control block§r - those cells come out as §cPLAIN CASING§r. Break the casing, put the real machine in.\n  §9the fuel pillars and rod loading ports§r inside the silo - optional interior, left as air.\nSteps 4 to 9 place all of it, and every one of them hands you part of the bill.\n\n§2§lDONE WHEN§r\nYou are holding the §964x Light Concrete§r and §916x Radiation Proof Machine Casing§r listed above. §8Steps 1 and 2 paid you exactly that. Claim this BEFORE you start projecting - in survival the projector eats blocks straight out of your pack as it works.§r\n\n§5CHECK YOUR WORK - THE PROJECTION IS FINISHED WHEN§r\nRight-clicking the controller with the projector places nothing more. The only cells still empty anywhere on the campus are then the §912 Turbine Housings§r and the silo interior.\n\n§cThose 12 ghosts never go solid, and you have not done anything wrong.§r The hologram draws them and always will; the survival projector skips them every single time, on purpose, because a housing carries a spin setting and a rotor it has no business guessing. Step 7 places all twelve by hand. Do not stand there clicking at them.\n\n§cThe controller is also still NOT FORMED at the end of this step.§r That is correct too. It is short of its §9Maintenance Hatch§r, its §9Feedwater Input Hatch§r, its §9Output Hatch§r and its §9Depleted Output Bus§r - four sockets, and they are the whole job of step 4. §6The plant forms at the end of step 4, not here.§r\n\n[note]Only the PLATFORM is mandatory. Silo, spine, spiral, gallery and towers are all optional pieces - but a platform on its own generates nothing, and a silo with no gallery is a steam EXPORT plant rather than a generator.[/note]",
